														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2119203">
									

<p>I think I actually prefer the previous version. I don't particularly care for the notion that some random German teacher was able to cobble these together out of dogs; it takes away from being able to contemplate what kind of twisted person would go to the trouble of making responsive whiteboards that feel pain. &quot;Ms. So-and-so because she wanted teaching aids for her German class&quot; is not really a satisfactory answer to that mystery for me.</p>
<p>Also, does this really need to be a &quot;bigger on the inside&quot; style spatial anomaly? That just feels kind of unnecessary. I can just imagine the German teacher at her house, merrily constructing these, and thinking to herself, &quot;hmm, I can't quite fit everything in here, I can either make the casing a little bigger, or BEND THE LAWS OF SPACE-TIME ITSELF&quot;. C'mon.</p>

							</div>

								
					
